  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 151 AM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nA hot and dry weather pattern is in store for much of next week as \nan upper-level ridge takes hold over the region. Ensemble guidance \nis in good agreement with the ridge staying over the region through \nat least late next week. Similar high temperatures each day are \nforecast in the mid 90s to low 100s for most locations. Spots along \nthe river valleys look to range from 105 to near 110. As of now, \nMonday offers the \"best\" shot of showers/storms over the mountains, \nthough overall chances remain low around 15%. From there, chances \ndwindle as the upper ridge parks over the region. Lows in the upper \n60s to mid 70s can be expected each night. \n\nLamberson",
